  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LO: Social Partners for Decent Work (2023-2025)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact: Workers and their families benefit from a well organised labour market characterised by high employment rates, decent wages and safe working environment in Ghana, Tunisia, Colombia and Vietnam.

Outcome 1: Social partners have jointly influenced national policies in line with the decent work agenda
Outcome 2: The climate for social dialogue has been improved in the focus countries
The project aims to contribute to increasing the rate of women participating in the work force in partner countries. LO/NHO will facilitate the transfer of knowledge on gender equality and key ILO gender equality conventions to inform social dialogue.

The direct target group is the sister organisations of LO and NHO (representative employers and workers&#x2019; organisations) in the focus countries (Vietnam, Tunisia, Ghana and Colombia). The project aims to contribute to increasing the rate of women participating in the work force in partner countries. LO/NHO will facilitate the transfer of knowledge on gender equality and key ILO gender equality conventions to inform social dialogue.</narrative>
  </description>
